# Open (Green's-function) z caps variant of the z-outflow test: same
# passive density pulse advecting out through z_hi, but the axial FIELD
# ghosts are now the free-space Green's fill instead of the solver's
# zero-gradient clamp (the fluid moments keep the Neumann outflow ghosts).
# The quiescent electromagnetic state (uniform external Bz, zero plasma
# response, E = -u x B = 0) has zero interior plasma current, so the
# Green's cap ghosts are exactly zero in the plasma-response frame and the
# pulse must exit exactly as it does through the Neumann ends: same
# analysis, same acceptance.
FILE = inputs_test_rz_theta_implicit_mhd_z_outflow_open

boundary.field_lo = none open
boundary.field_hi = open open
